{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal model combining scvi_n200 RNA encoding, resnet50 image encoding, avgpool aggregation, and concat fusion, building on the RNA-only best configuration (config_005). Validation accuracy of 0.6315 is slightly lower than the RNA-only baseline (0.6529), suggesting image modality addition may not improve performance. Validation F1 (0.6068) aligns with RNA-only results, indicating potential but inconclusive evidence of multimodal benefits. Uncertainty remains about the impact of image modality, fusion strategy, and whether alternative encoders or aggregation methods could yield different outcomes."
}

